+            .displayName("File Mime Type")
+            .description("Mime type of the file to be uploaded." +
+                    " The property value will only be used if 'Upload FlowFile' has been set to 'Yes'." +
+                    " If the property evaluated to null or empty string, then the mime type will be set to 'application/octet-stream' in the Slack message.")
+            .defaultValue("${" + CoreAttributes.MIME_TYPE.key() + "}")
+            .addValidator(StandardValidators.NON_EMPTY_VALIDATOR)
+            .expressionLanguageSupported(ExpressionLanguageScope.FLOWFILE_ATTRIBUTES)
+            .build();
+
+    public static final PropertyDescriptor USERNAME = new PropertyDescriptor

 Review comment:
   It's unfortunate that Slack doesn't match the username in the API call to the access token for that user. With this property, it is possible to spoof someone else's username, emoji, etc. Is it possible to use the token to retrieve the user information via the API, rather than asking the flow designer to provide the user info? I didn't see a way, so maybe we should hardcode it to something using `this.getIdentifier()` and `Thread.currentThread().getName()`? It would be a long awkward name but would prevent spoofing. What do you think?

