+                    " If the property evaluated to null or empty string, then the mime type will be set to 'application/octet-stream' in the Slack message.")
+            .defaultValue("${" + CoreAttributes.MIME_TYPE.key() + "}")
+            .addValidator(StandardValidators.NON_EMPTY_VALIDATOR)
+            .expressionLanguageSupported(ExpressionLanguageScope.FLOWFILE_ATTRIBUTES)
+            .build();
+
+    public static final PropertyDescriptor USERNAME = new PropertyDescriptor

 Review comment:
   In order to prevent spoofing, we need to remove the username as a configurable property by the end user.

   Regarding the instance/thread id logging: do you mean our nifi logs or also sending this id to Slack as the username?
   In the second case this long technical id would be displayed in Slack which not really user friendly I think. I would prefer to see in Slack that "Whatever App/Bot" sent me a message rather than an id. So I would use the App name for this (which is the default).

