 Review comment:
   If it gets here, I don't know what happened but likely some external environment (I/O) issue. Rollback does not use more disk space; it does do I/O to reset the journal removing bytes at the end.

   It is a log message so won't be seen until later.

   "System unstable" was supposed to communicate that.

   How about changing it to include "contact users@jena" and making it a `java.lang.Error`?


