column360:
21/Feb/19 12:17;shashikant;Thanks[~elek] for the patch. I think 
{code:java}
RandomKeyGenerator.java:

  try (Scope writeScope = GlobalTracer.get()
+                    .buildSpan("writeKeyData")
+                    .startActive(true)) {
+                  os.write(keyValue);
+                  os.write(randomValue);
+                }
                 os.close();

{code}
I think, os.close() should also be under the trace scope as close will actually flush the data residing in the buffer if its less than a chunk size and then waits for the ack from Ratis. 

Usually , for keys less than a chunk size(16 MB), this is os.close() is where the data will be written to the datanode and we will wait for the write to happen to atleast majority of nodes.

