If using JNDI one has to make client code depend on JNDI plus we have to remove connection from directory service when it is closed (to avoid memory leaks). 

It seems to create more problems than solving. 

{quote}
There’s nothing stopping you from creating schemas (or trees of schemas) manually. And yes, you can put whatever kinds of objects you like as constructor parameters for your schema. But if you want to use SchemaFactory, or model JSON, or you want your plan to be instantiable in a different context or VM, you have to play by the rules.
